    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you help me with a depreciation calc? I have a piece of equipment that cost $45,000. It has an estimated salvage value of $5,000 and a useful life of 8 years. I need to find the annual straight-line depreciation amount. Can you walk me through the steps?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To calculate straight-line depreciation, you first subtract the salvage value from the initial cost to find the depreciable base: $45,000 - $5,000 = $40,000. Next, you divide this amount by the useful life of the asset: $40,000 ÷ 8 years = $5,000. The resulting figure represents the annual depreciation expense. Therefore, your equipment will depreciate by $5,000 each year over its 8-year lifespan.",
      "source": "target",
