      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you are correct; the straight-line method results in the same depreciation amount every year regardless of actual usage. While methods like \"switching costs,\" which account for heavier wear and tear in early years, offer a more realistic picture of usage, straight-line is preferred by most industries and tax authorities for its simplicity and predictability. This predictable schedule makes financial reporting easier for budgeting and tax planning, whereas alternative methods provide a less structured view of asset value over time.",
      "source": "target",
